WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:14.000
Ladies and gentlemen, the story you are about to see is true.

00:30.000 --> 00:37.000
This is the city.

00:37.000 --> 00:41.000
Los Angeles, California.

00:41.000 --> 00:43.000
I work here.

00:43.000 --> 00:45.000
I'm a cop.

00:45.000 --> 00:50.000
It was Wednesday, December 24th.

00:50.000 --> 00:52.000
We were working the day watch out of Berkley Division.

00:52.000 --> 00:54.000
The boss is Captain Bernard.

00:54.000 --> 00:55.000
My partner is Frank Smith.

00:55.000 --> 01:05.000
My name is Friday.

01:05.000 --> 01:06.000
Hi, Joe.

01:06.000 --> 01:08.000
Hi.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.000
Christmas cards, huh?

01:09.000 --> 01:10.000
A little late, aren't you?

01:10.000 --> 01:13.000
Well, I was going to send them out Monday, but we had that stakeout.

01:13.000 --> 01:15.000
You ought to get married, Joe.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.000
Yeah?

01:16.000 --> 01:18.000
It's the only system.

01:18.000 --> 01:19.000
They does all the stuff for me.

01:19.000 --> 01:21.000
Laundry, mail, cards.

01:21.000 --> 01:22.000
Only system.

01:22.000 --> 01:24.000
Might help.

01:24.000 --> 01:25.000
Got a big stack there.

01:25.000 --> 01:27.000
Ought to cut down the list.

01:27.000 --> 01:28.000
Look at this here.

01:28.000 --> 01:29.000
Upholstery shop.

01:29.000 --> 01:30.000
Yeah?

01:30.000 --> 01:31.000
They send me a card every year.

01:31.000 --> 01:32.000
I never get anything upholstered.

01:32.000 --> 01:34.000
Fay and I ought to go over our list.

01:34.000 --> 01:36.000
Cut off a few names.

01:36.000 --> 01:38.000
I brought in your present.

01:38.000 --> 01:39.000
Want to open it now?

01:39.000 --> 01:40.000
No, I'll wait.

01:40.000 --> 01:42.000
I always open a couple a day before.

01:42.000 --> 01:43.000
Why?

01:43.000 --> 01:45.000
Well, it puts you in the spirit ahead of time.

01:45.000 --> 01:47.000
I opened Phil's this morning.

01:47.000 --> 01:48.000
Who's he?

01:48.000 --> 01:49.000
Fay's brother in Denver.

01:49.000 --> 01:50.000
Gave me a magazine.

01:50.000 --> 01:51.000
One of those funny ones.

01:51.000 --> 01:52.000
What do you mean?

01:52.000 --> 01:53.000
A comic book?

01:53.000 --> 01:55.000
No, one of those funny ones, you know.

01:55.000 --> 01:56.000
No, I don't, Frank.

01:56.000 --> 01:59.000
Well, some of the pages have holes in them.

01:59.000 --> 02:01.000
You look through and there's a picture on the next page.

02:01.000 --> 02:03.000
Oh, yeah, I've seen those on the newsstand.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.000
They have cloth pasted in.

02:05.000 --> 02:06.000
Cloth?

02:06.000 --> 02:07.000
In the ads.

02:07.000 --> 02:09.000
If you want to buy a suit, they have a sample right there.

02:09.000 --> 02:10.000
You mean you can feel it?

02:10.000 --> 02:12.000
Reach right out and feel it.

02:12.000 --> 02:13.000
There was one for $200.

02:13.000 --> 02:14.000
A suit?

02:14.000 --> 02:15.000
Sure.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.000
Cloth comes from Scotland.

02:16.000 --> 02:18.000
What's it made out of, solid gold?

02:18.000 --> 02:20.000
No, they got a special kind of gold over there.

02:20.000 --> 02:21.000
It's real smooth.

02:21.000 --> 02:22.000
Not a goat, Frank, a sheep.

02:22.000 --> 02:26.000
Well, a special kind of sheep, then, because a suit costs $200.

02:26.000 --> 02:27.000
You going to get one?

02:27.000 --> 02:28.000
I told Fay.

02:28.000 --> 02:30.000
She said wear the sample.

02:30.000 --> 02:31.000
Anything to it?

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
Fanning and Pryor were in on that market holdup.

02:33.000 --> 02:34.000
They come up with anything?

02:34.000 --> 02:36.000
Pound of air, nothing else.

02:36.000 --> 02:37.000
I hope it stays quiet.

02:37.000 --> 02:39.000
I've got more shopping to do.

02:39.000 --> 02:40.000
I finished.

02:40.000 --> 02:41.000
What did you get Ann?

02:41.000 --> 02:45.000
Stationery set, some paper and envelopes, leather binding.

02:45.000 --> 02:47.000
Joe, you'll never learn.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.000
What's the matter?

02:48.000 --> 02:50.000
No woman wants a stationary set.

02:50.000 --> 02:51.000
Get her something personal.

02:51.000 --> 02:53.000
Well, it's got her initials on it.

02:53.000 --> 02:57.000
No, no, you want something more sentimental, romantic.

02:57.000 --> 02:59.000
What did you get Fay?

02:59.000 --> 03:00.000
It's different in her case.

03:00.000 --> 03:02.000
What did you get Fay?

03:02.000 --> 03:04.000
Sewing machine.

03:04.000 --> 03:05.000
That's romantic.

03:05.000 --> 03:07.000
Well, there's no way.

03:07.000 --> 03:09.000
Why don't you buy her a catcher's mitt?

03:09.000 --> 03:15.000
Gregory Friday.

03:15.000 --> 03:16.000
Yes, that's right.

03:16.000 --> 03:19.000
You have the right department.

03:19.000 --> 03:21.000
All right, father, we'll be right down.

03:21.000 --> 03:23.000
No, you can tell us about it there.

03:23.000 --> 03:24.000
Goodbye.

03:24.000 --> 03:26.000
The old mission church, they've had a theft.

03:26.000 --> 03:27.000
Collection money?

03:27.000 --> 03:48.000
Statue of the child Jesus.

03:48.000 --> 04:00.000
Frank and I checked out of the office and rode over to the church at the corner of Sunset Boulevard and Main Street near the Union Station.

04:00.000 --> 04:05.000
It was an old church that was there before there was a Union Station or trains to come into a station.

04:05.000 --> 04:19.000
The Padres from down in Mexico built it. The devout Mexicans in town still attended services there.

04:19.000 --> 04:44.000
At 10.05 a.m., we asked for Father Xavier Rojas, who had communicated with us. We were told he was inside.

04:44.000 --> 04:51.000
We found Father Rojas up near the sanctuary. He told us about the crib. It was a $70 duplication of the scene at Bethlehem.

04:51.000 --> 04:54.000
The parishioners had taken up a collection for it 31 years ago.

04:54.000 --> 04:59.000
It was put up every year on December 22nd and taken down after the holy season.

04:59.000 --> 05:27.000
It was beautiful, except that one of the shepherds had lost an arm, a sheep was old and cracked, and the infant Jesus was missing.

05:27.000 --> 05:31.000
Father, especially now, the holiday season, we cash our checks, Father.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.000
You want to tell us what happened, or what you think happened?

05:34.000 --> 05:37.000
I discovered the statue was missing right after the six o'clock mass.

05:37.000 --> 05:38.000
You say the six?

05:38.000 --> 05:41.000
Yes. I started over to the rectory and stopped by the crib.

05:41.000 --> 05:43.000
Was the statue there before mass?

05:43.000 --> 05:45.000
I don't know, but it was there last night.

05:45.000 --> 05:47.000
How late is the church open?

05:47.000 --> 05:52.000
All night. We leave it wide open so any thief can walk in, particularly thieves, Sergeant.

05:52.000 --> 05:56.000
You say it was there last night, Father, how late?

05:56.000 --> 05:58.000
Ten or eleven o'clock we had confessions.

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
No one saw it after that?

06:00.000 --> 06:03.000
One of the altar boys. He says it may have been there. He thinks it was.

06:03.000 --> 06:04.000
Did he see it?

06:04.000 --> 06:05.000
He's not sure.

06:05.000 --> 06:06.000
What's his name?

06:06.000 --> 06:07.000
Pardon me.

06:12.000 --> 06:15.000
Here's the schedule. You'll find the names for every mass there.

06:15.000 --> 06:17.000
Was there a big crowd at the six o'clock mass, Father?

06:17.000 --> 06:20.000
Not too many. Seven's the big one. People on their way to work.

06:20.000 --> 06:22.000
Did anyone stay after mass, did you notice?

06:22.000 --> 06:28.000
Not especially. I came back here, took off the vestments. I suppose it was ten or fifteen minutes before I went back into church.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.000
It was empty then?

06:29.000 --> 06:31.000
No. People were coming in for the seven o'clock.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.000
Are these the altar boys, James Corneen and Joseph Heffernan?

06:34.000 --> 06:37.000
That's right. Joe's the one who mentioned it might have been there.

06:37.000 --> 06:38.000
Did you check with the other priests, Father?

06:38.000 --> 06:41.000
Before I called you. None of them knows anything about it.

06:41.000 --> 06:44.000
Just for a check on the pawn shops, how much did the statue worth?

06:44.000 --> 06:45.000
In money.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.000
What's the point in pawn shops, Father?

06:47.000 --> 06:49.000
Only a few dollars.

06:49.000 --> 06:52.000
We could get a new one, but it wouldn't be the same.

06:52.000 --> 06:56.000
We've had children in the parish. They've grown up and married.

06:56.000 --> 06:58.000
It's the only Jesus they know.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.000
I understand.

06:59.000 --> 07:03.000
And we've had children who died. It was the only Jesus they knew.

07:03.000 --> 07:06.000
So many of the people who come here are simple people.

07:06.000 --> 07:10.000
They wouldn't understand, Sergeant. It would be like changing the evening star.

07:10.000 --> 07:11.000
We'll do our best, Father.

07:11.000 --> 07:15.000
That's why it would mean so much to have it back for the first mass on Christmas.

07:15.000 --> 07:17.000
Not very long, Father.

07:17.000 --> 07:18.000
Less than twenty-four hours.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.000
If anything turns up here, you know where to get in touch with us.

07:21.000 --> 07:22.000
Yes.

07:23.000 --> 07:24.000
Sad, isn't it?

07:24.000 --> 07:25.000
How's that?

07:25.000 --> 07:27.000
In so short a time, men learn to steal.

07:27.000 --> 07:29.000
Yes, but consider us, Father.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.000
Us?

07:30.000 --> 07:33.000
If some of them didn't, you and I'd be out of work.

07:33.000 --> 07:36.000
1050 A.M.

07:46.000 --> 07:49.000
1050 A.M. We notified Pawn Shop Detail.

07:49.000 --> 07:53.000
We gave them a description of the missing object, the time and the place of theft.

07:53.000 --> 07:57.000
A few minutes later, Frank and I checked out the two altar boys.

07:57.000 --> 08:00.000
The first one, James Corneen, said that he knew nothing about it.

08:00.000 --> 08:04.000
After mass, he'd gone out the sacristy door and come straight home for breakfast.

08:05.000 --> 08:08.000
The second one, Joseph Heffernan, was not at home.

08:08.000 --> 08:10.000
His father said he had a part-time job.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
He'd have him get in touch with us after lunch.

08:12.000 --> 08:15.000
By 1130 A.M., we'd run out of book procedure.

08:15.000 --> 08:16.000
We had a man to find.

08:16.000 --> 08:19.000
Our only clue, he'd been to church.

08:25.000 --> 08:27.000
We're police officers.

08:27.000 --> 08:29.000
My name's Friday. This is my partner, Frank Smith.

08:29.000 --> 08:31.000
Good to see you. Caught me in the middle of a big chess match.

08:31.000 --> 08:32.000
Where's your partner?

08:32.000 --> 08:34.000
Up in San Jose. We've been playing for years.

08:34.000 --> 08:35.000
I see.

08:35.000 --> 08:38.000
You know, we do it through the mail. I send him a move, he sends me one.

08:38.000 --> 08:39.000
You Mr. Flavin?

08:39.000 --> 08:41.000
How'd you know? We never met.

08:41.000 --> 08:42.000
Your name's on the window out front.

08:42.000 --> 08:46.000
Mr. Flavin, we checked the other two religious stores in this neighborhood. They're closed.

08:46.000 --> 08:49.000
This is the best one, anyway. 50% European items.

08:49.000 --> 08:51.000
We're checking the stores around the mission church.

08:51.000 --> 08:52.000
For what?

08:52.000 --> 08:54.000
Statue of the Child Jesus. Do you have one with you?

08:54.000 --> 08:57.000
Sure.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.000
No, sir. A larger one.

09:07.000 --> 09:10.000
You don't want a larger one. Unless it's for a church, that's where you want a larger one.

09:10.000 --> 09:26.000
Could we see it, please?

09:26.000 --> 09:28.000
Not my do to butt in.

09:28.000 --> 09:31.000
But unless you live in a big place, this'll make your living room all the kilder.

09:31.000 --> 09:32.000
Yes, sir.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.000
Do most of the people who go to the mission church trade here?

09:34.000 --> 09:36.000
Good many of them. Especially the kids.

09:36.000 --> 09:37.000
Why kids?

09:37.000 --> 09:38.000
More religious.

09:38.000 --> 09:41.000
Check on yourself. See if kids aren't more religious than you.

09:41.000 --> 09:42.000
Gladly so.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.000
That's what's wrong with the world.

09:43.000 --> 09:45.000
Oh, I don't mean you're wrong with it. Everybody.

09:45.000 --> 09:46.000
Yes, sir.

09:46.000 --> 09:48.000
What if we could stick to the point, Mr. Flavin?

09:48.000 --> 09:50.000
Sure. A lot of people from the mission church come in here.

09:50.000 --> 09:52.000
Do people ever come in and sell back a religious article?

09:52.000 --> 09:54.000
Like a prayer book or rosaries?

09:54.000 --> 09:55.000
Yes, sir.

09:55.000 --> 09:56.000
Secondhand, you mean?

09:56.000 --> 09:57.000
Yes, sir.

09:57.000 --> 09:59.000
Not since I ever been around. It's silly.

09:59.000 --> 10:00.000
Why?

10:00.000 --> 10:03.000
People don't have religious articles so they can get rid of them. They have them so they can have them.

10:03.000 --> 10:06.000
But if a man had a statue and wanted to sell it, he'd come to a place like this.

10:06.000 --> 10:08.000
Sure, but he wouldn't want to sell it.

10:08.000 --> 10:09.000
He would if it was stolen.

10:09.000 --> 10:13.000
No, sir. If a man was to steal a statue, he'd be crazy or something like that.

10:13.000 --> 10:15.000
The only place he'd want to go is where crazy people are.

10:15.000 --> 10:17.000
You may be right, Mr. Flavin.

10:17.000 --> 10:21.000
I don't know what you fellows are looking for, but if it's somebody who stole a statue, he's crazy and you won't find him.

10:21.000 --> 10:24.000
You won't find him as long as you live. Or in a million years.

10:24.000 --> 10:38.000
That should cover it.

10:38.000 --> 10:41.000
We continued to check religious stores out as far as Van Ness.

10:41.000 --> 10:47.000
We asked the same questions. The owners gave us the same answers, but none of them were as encouraging as Mr. Flavin.

10:47.000 --> 10:51.000
Frank and I had lunch and reported back to the office. It was 1.30 p.m.

10:51.000 --> 10:54.000
I just checked, Frank, our lunchroom. We've been out on a theft of the mission.

10:54.000 --> 10:56.000
Make it some action on the Patterson case.

10:56.000 --> 10:57.000
They locate him?

10:57.000 --> 10:58.000
They think he's on the bus from Sacramento.

10:58.000 --> 11:00.000
Well, that means the Bakersfield police.

11:00.000 --> 11:10.000
We'll wait and see.

11:10.000 --> 11:12.000
Are one of you fellows Sergeant Freddy?

11:12.000 --> 11:13.000
He is.

11:13.000 --> 11:16.000
I'm Jew Heffnan. My father said you wanted to see me.

11:16.000 --> 11:19.000
Sit down, son. You didn't have to come in. A phone call would have worked.

11:19.000 --> 11:24.000
My father said to get on over. He says that any kid that uses phones is lazy.

11:24.000 --> 11:27.000
We want to ask you about this morning. You serve 6 o'clock mass?

11:27.000 --> 11:30.000
Yes, sir. I'm senior boy, so I get the 6.

11:30.000 --> 11:32.000
You're senior and you take the early trick?

11:32.000 --> 11:36.000
Yes, sir. That way, if you receive communion, you get to have breakfast sooner.

11:36.000 --> 11:39.000
Father Rojas says you think the statue was there before mass.

11:39.000 --> 11:42.000
I didn't look, but I have a feeling it was there.

11:42.000 --> 11:43.000
A feeling?

11:43.000 --> 11:47.000
You know, how you have a feeling about something, but you're not sure.

11:47.000 --> 11:49.000
Were you not sure?

11:49.000 --> 11:50.000
Did you stay around long after mass?

11:50.000 --> 11:52.000
I put out candles and hung up my surplus.

11:52.000 --> 11:54.000
How long would that take?

11:54.000 --> 11:55.000
About 5 minutes, maybe.

11:55.000 --> 11:57.000
Did any of the people at mass stay on?

11:57.000 --> 12:00.000
Some moms do, especially ladies.

12:00.000 --> 12:01.000
Oh.

12:01.000 --> 12:05.000
Maybe they don't finish in time, or else they start new prayers. I don't know.

12:05.000 --> 12:07.000
So when you left, there were still some women there?

12:07.000 --> 12:09.000
No, sir. That was at first.

12:09.000 --> 12:13.000
After I went back to the sacristy, there was only this one man.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.000
What man?

12:14.000 --> 12:15.000
He comes at 6 o'clock all the time.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.000
Do you know his name?

12:16.000 --> 12:17.000
No, sir.

12:17.000 --> 12:19.000
But he works down in Olive.

12:19.000 --> 12:21.000
You know, paint shop, where they paint signs.

12:21.000 --> 12:23.000
Could you describe him?

12:23.000 --> 12:24.000
Sort of medium.

12:24.000 --> 12:26.000
He was wearing a suit that didn't match.

12:26.000 --> 12:27.000
Didn't match?

12:27.000 --> 12:29.000
You know, different pants than coat.

12:29.000 --> 12:30.000
How about his age?

12:30.000 --> 12:31.000
Oh, he's pretty old.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.000
Take a guess.

12:32.000 --> 12:34.000
About 40, maybe.

12:34.000 --> 12:36.000
There's nothing particular about him.

12:36.000 --> 12:37.000
Then why did you notice him?

12:37.000 --> 12:38.000
I've seen him before.

12:38.000 --> 12:40.000
In the bundle, I guess.

12:40.000 --> 12:41.000
The bundle?

12:41.000 --> 12:42.000
Out in front.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.000
I saw him when he was coming out.

12:43.000 --> 12:45.000
He had this bundle, and he almost dropped it.

12:45.000 --> 12:47.000
How large a bundle?

12:47.000 --> 12:48.000
It's hard to say.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.000
Come on, son.

12:49.000 --> 12:51.000
Was it large or small, the size of the statue?

12:51.000 --> 12:52.000
Not that big.

12:52.000 --> 12:53.000
Yes, sir.

13:06.000 --> 13:07.000
We located the sign shop.

13:07.000 --> 13:11.000
The suspect didn't work there anymore, but we discovered his name was Claude Stroop.

13:11.000 --> 13:13.000
We found out where he lived.

13:13.000 --> 13:16.000
225 PM, we arrived there.

13:16.000 --> 13:20.000
It was a hotel for men, mostly old men, mostly down on hours.

13:20.000 --> 13:22.000
It was called the Golden Dream.

13:24.000 --> 13:25.000
Police officers.

13:25.000 --> 13:27.000
We're looking for Claude Stroop.

13:27.000 --> 13:28.000
Hope Claude didn't get in any trouble.

13:28.000 --> 13:29.000
So do we. Is he in?

13:29.000 --> 13:30.000
No.

13:30.000 --> 13:31.000
He's got room 307.

13:31.000 --> 13:32.000
You can check if you like.

13:32.000 --> 13:33.000
We'll take your word.

13:33.000 --> 13:34.000
Were you on this morning?

13:34.000 --> 13:35.000
Hmm?

13:35.000 --> 13:36.000
Yeah, the early shift.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.000
Well, we don't have shifts.

13:37.000 --> 13:39.000
My uncle owns the place.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.000
I'm the shift.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.000
Did Stroop spend last night here?

13:41.000 --> 13:42.000
Came in about 11.

13:42.000 --> 13:43.000
When did he leave this morning?

13:43.000 --> 13:44.000
Around 6, maybe before.

13:44.000 --> 13:45.000
He come back after?

13:45.000 --> 13:47.000
8 o'clock or so, then left.

13:47.000 --> 13:48.000
Supposed to be back at 10.

13:48.000 --> 13:50.000
And pulls this trick.

13:50.000 --> 13:51.000
What trick?

13:51.000 --> 13:52.000
A program.

13:52.000 --> 13:53.000
He knows the other fellas need him.

13:53.000 --> 13:54.000
Program?

13:54.000 --> 13:57.000
Here at the hotel, every Christmas we have a program.

13:57.000 --> 13:58.000
Put up a tree and sing.

13:58.000 --> 14:00.000
They're mostly old fellas.

14:00.000 --> 14:03.000
Singing like that makes them remember back when they were kids.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.000
Then Jimmy Finn comes on.

14:04.000 --> 14:05.000
Jimmy Finn?

14:05.000 --> 14:07.000
He shares number 409.

14:07.000 --> 14:10.000
His family once had a lot of money, so he tells the fellas about it.

14:10.000 --> 14:12.000
Stories about Christmas.

14:12.000 --> 14:15.000
How they had this big log and his grandfather used to start it up.

14:15.000 --> 14:20.000
After dinner, everybody turned over his plate and there underneath was a $20 gold piece.

14:20.000 --> 14:22.000
Brand new one.

14:22.000 --> 14:24.000
When Stroop came in this morning, did he have a bundle?

14:24.000 --> 14:25.000
I didn't see him come in.

14:25.000 --> 14:26.000
You said you saw him.

14:26.000 --> 14:28.000
I saw him go out after, but not come in.

14:28.000 --> 14:29.000
When was that?

14:29.000 --> 14:30.000
8.

14:30.000 --> 14:32.000
If you want to look for a bundle, I could give you his key.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.000
